{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>But only the matter</b> — One might think that if he wishes to curse the nations he may curse Israel along with them, or if he wishes to bless Israel he may bless the idolatrous nations as well. Therefore it says: 'אך חלק' (but only a portion) — a division."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The phrase 'אך חלק' is read as a limiter: Balaam may address only one party at a time, not bless or curse both together. 'ת\"ל' = ת\"ל (תא בעינן למימר / 'come and learn') introducing the limiting verse. 'העכו\"ם ג\"כ' expanded as העובדי כוכבים ומזלות גם כן (the star-worshipping nations as well)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:51.841786355Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}